<article class="help-card {{ $topic === 'google_verification' ? 'selected' : '' }}" id="google-verification"><span class="eyebrow">GOOGLE SEARCH CONSOLE</span><h2>Google verification</h2><p class="where"><strong>Go to:</strong> <a href="https://search.google.com/search-console" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Search Console ↗</a></p><ol><li>Sign in with the Google account that should own the website.</li><li>Click <strong>Add property</strong> and enter your website address. For a simple start, use the URL-prefix property with your full site URL.</li><li>Open the ownership verification screen and choose <strong>HTML tag</strong>.</li><li>Google will show a meta tag similar to <code>&lt;meta name="google-site-verification" content="YOUR_VALUE"&gt;</code>.</li><li>Copy <strong>only the value inside content="..."</strong>. Do not copy the full HTML tag.</li><li>Return to this website → <strong>Admin → Settings → SEO &amp; Integrations</strong>.</li><li>Paste the value into <strong>Google Search Console verification</strong>, then click <strong>Save SEO settings</strong>.</li><li>Go back to Google Search Console and click <strong>Verify</strong>.</li></ol><p class="tip"><strong>If verification fails:</strong> make sure the value is exact, the website is publicly accessible, and you saved the setting before clicking Verify. Google documents the HTML-tag method and its troubleshooting steps in its ownership guide.</p><a class="doc-link" href="https://support.google.com/webmasters/answer/9008080" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Google's official verification guide ↗</a></article>
<article class="help-card {{ $topic === 'bing_verification' ? 'selected' : '' }}" id="bing-verification"><span class="eyebrow">BING WEBMASTER</span><h2>Bing verification</h2><p class="where"><strong>Go to:</strong> <a href="https://www.bing.com/webmasters" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bing Webmaster Tools ↗</a></p><ol><li>Sign in to Bing Webmaster Tools with your Microsoft account.</li><li>Add your website and open its <strong>Verify ownership</strong> options.</li><li>Choose the <strong>HTML Meta Tag</strong> verification method when it is offered.</li><li>Copy the verification value Bing provides for the <code>content</code> attribute.</li><li>Return to this website → <strong>Admin → Settings → SEO &amp; Integrations</strong>.</li><li>Paste that value into <strong>Bing Webmaster verification</strong> and click <strong>Save SEO settings</strong>.</li><li>Return to Bing Webmaster Tools and complete the ownership verification.</li></ol><p class="tip"><strong>Important:</strong> paste the verification value, not a password and not the complete HTML tag, unless Bing explicitly instructs you otherwise.</p><a class="doc-link" href="https://www.bing.com/webmasters" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Bing Webmaster Tools ↗</a></article>
<article class="help-card {{ $topic === 'meta_verification' ? 'selected' : '' }}" id="meta-verification"><span class="eyebrow">META / FACEBOOK</span><h2>Meta domain verification</h2><p class="where"><strong>Go to:</strong> <a href="https://business.facebook.com/settings/domains" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Meta Business Settings → Domains ↗</a></p><ol><li>Sign in to the Meta Business account that manages your organization.</li><li>Open <strong>Business Settings → Brand Safety → Domains</strong> (Meta may adjust the menu wording).</li><li>Add or select your website domain.</li><li>Choose the <strong>Meta-tag verification</strong> method if it is available for your domain.</li><li>Meta will provide a verification meta tag/value. Copy the verification value exactly as provided.</li><li>Return to this website → <strong>Admin → Settings → SEO &amp; Integrations</strong>.</li><li>Paste the value into <strong>Meta domain verification</strong> and click <strong>Save SEO settings</strong>.</li><li>Return to Meta and click the button to verify the domain.</li></ol><p class="tip"><strong>Optional:</strong> only configure this field if your organization actually uses Meta domain verification. If Meta gives you a DNS or file-based method instead, follow Meta's method-specific instructions rather than putting unrelated DNS values into this field.</p><a class="doc-link" href="https://business.facebook.com/settings/domains" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Meta domain settings ↗</a></article>
<article class="help-card {{ $topic === 'ga4_measurement_id' ? 'selected' : '' }}" id="ga4-measurement-id"><span class="eyebrow">GOOGLE ANALYTICS 4</span><h2>GA4 Measurement ID</h2><p class="where"><strong>Go to:</strong> <a href="https://analytics.google.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Analytics ↗</a></p><ol><li>Sign in to Google Analytics and select the correct property for this website.</li><li>Click <strong>Admin</strong>.</li><li>Under <strong>Data collection and modification</strong>, click <strong>Data streams</strong>.</li><li>Choose <strong>Web</strong>, then click the web data stream for this website.</li><li>In the stream details, find <strong>Measurement ID</strong>. It normally starts with <code>G-</code>.</li><li>Copy the complete ID, for example <code>G-XXXXXXXXXX</code>.</li><li>Return to this website → <strong>Admin → Settings → SEO &amp; Integrations</strong>.</li><li>Paste it into <strong>GA4 Measurement ID</strong> and click <strong>Save SEO settings</strong>.</li><li>After the website receives traffic, use GA4 <strong>Realtime</strong> to confirm that data is arriving.</li></ol><p class="tip"><strong>Do not paste:</strong> your Google password, property number, stream ID, or the full Google tag code. This field expects the Measurement ID beginning with <code>G-</code>.</p><a class="doc-link" href="https://support.google.com/analytics/answer/12270356" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Google's official Measurement ID guide ↗</a></article>
<article class="help-card {{ $topic === 'indexnow_key' ? 'selected' : '' }}" id="indexnow-key"><span class="eyebrow">INDEXNOW</span><h2>IndexNow API key</h2><p class="where"><strong>Learn more:</strong> <a href="https://www.indexnow.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IndexNow.org ↗</a></p><ol><li>Create or generate a unique IndexNow key for this website using an IndexNow-compatible tool or provider.</li><li>Make sure the key is intended for this website and follows the allowed format shown in this settings page.</li><li>Return to this website → <strong>Admin → Settings → SEO &amp; Integrations</strong>.</li><li>Paste the key into <strong>IndexNow API key</strong> and click <strong>Save SEO settings</strong>.</li><li>This system exposes the verification file at <code>https://fuelfreepowerplant.com/indexnow/{key}.txt</code> after saving.</li><li>Replace <code>{key}</code> with the exact key you saved and open that URL in a browser. The page should return the key as plain text.</li><li>Use that same key with an IndexNow-compatible submission workflow to notify supported search engines about changed URLs.</li><li>Check the provider's response or diagnostics to confirm that the URL notification was accepted.</li></ol><p class="tip"><strong>Security note:</strong> an IndexNow key is intentionally public for verification. Never use your database password, hosting password, or an unrelated private API secret here.</p><a class="doc-link" href="https://www.indexnow.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open the official IndexNow site ↗</a></article>
<article class="help-card security {{ $topic === 'security' ? 'selected' : '' }}"><span class="eyebrow">SECURITY</span><h2>What belongs in these fields?</h2><p>These settings are for identifiers and verification values that are designed to appear in the website's public integration layer. Never paste passwords, database credentials, private OAuth secrets, hosting credentials, or unrelated private API secrets.</p><p>If a future integration requires a genuinely secret credential, it should be stored server-side with appropriate encryption/access controls and must never be printed into public HTML.</p></article>
